Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 23:42:03 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 61/62] hjviewer: the access password's screens (staff-only
 gate)

Whoever does not log in enters the access password the operator set
(hjviewer's docs/access-tickets.md 3-5, 5-3), and the app trades it with
POST /api/hjv/guest for one PC's ticket, then forgets it:

- src/hjviewer_access/guest.rs seals the password for the purpose "guest",
  with the use and the PC it reaches, by the server's clock (once more
  after a 409 clock), and signs a PC's request with the device key over
  the seal ("hjv-guest-pc-v1"). Its tests pin hjv-api's README vector.
- A controller's ticket stays in this process's memory for its target
  and goes with the last session to it (session_close), so a new
  connection asks again and the session's own reconnections do not. A
  PC's goes over the IPC (Data::HjvGuestPc) to the process that
  registers, in memory only; it ends with that process or in 12 hours.
- The screens ask through main_set_common, which waits for the exchange,
  and read its result with main_get_common.
- Flutter: hbbs's refusal (msgbox hjv-access-error) opens A1 for an app
  without a login, with [Log in], [Connect with the access password] and
  [Cancel], and shows A2 as an error box to a logged-in one. The PC home
  (also the quick support window) shows P1 while hbbs refuses this PC's
  registration, with [Log in] and [Access password] (P2). Settings and the
  install page say that an unattended PC must stay logged in (G1). Texts in
  Korean and English; their choices are tested without the bridge.
- The app's start and each return to the front wake the renewing thread
  of the login's ticket (hjv-access-refresh), as 0058 left for the screens.
- E2E: HJV_E2E_ACCESS_PASSWORD for the connect commands and
  --hjv-e2e-guest-pc <password>; exit code 6 when no ticket came.

A server that checks nothing (MODE=off) refuses nobody, so the screens
stay as they were; a build that is not an account build carries nothing.

Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01UGRoRVHEhxg8GAbP842qdV
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
